<div class="callout callout-insight">
  <span class="callout-icon">💡</span>
  <span>The draft model must be <em>extremely fast</em> — otherwise the overhead of drafting cancels the parallel-verification win. Gemma 4's assistant achieves this by reusing the backbone's KV cache and operating at a much smaller hidden dimension.</span>
</div>
</section>

<!-- ─────────────────────────────────── §2 Architecture -->
<section id="s-arch" data-code="architecture">
<div class="section-no">02 — Architecture</div>
<h2>The two-model system</h2>
<p>
  The system consists of <code>Gemma4ForCausalLM</code> (the backbone) and <code>Gemma4AssistantForCausalLM</code> (the draft model). The backbone runs a standard forward pass and writes the K/V states from its <strong>last non-sharing layer of each attention type</strong> into <code>shared_kv_states</code>. The assistant reads those two tensors to draft tokens without recomputing attention from scratch.
</p>
